# swarm (D152): the swarm file and this node's roles in it (swarm(4)),
# in the cpu images, whose nodes make a swarm. It keeps the file on the
# node's volume, tells cs to reread it, asks 9gate to listen for the
# `file` role, and listens on tcp!*!17020 for the members' pushes, its
# handshakes through factotum, granted the node's noise-ik key (D75).
# On tcp!*!17021 it answers other nodes' swarm slots (D153), with the
# node's mcr key, which factotum also holds.
service swarm
program swarm
use net
use cs
use 9gate
use factotum
grant factotum proto=noise-ik
grant factotum proto=mcr
mount /net net/net
mount /net cs/net after
mount /data fs/volume create
export
restart on-failure
